<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</h1><p class="st-meta">1701 CE – 1918 CE · capital Schwerin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The larger Mecklenburg state on the Baltic, ruled by one of Europe's oldest dynasties and known for its archaic feudal constitution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the extinction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustrow">Güstrow</a> line in 1695, a succession dispute in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-mecklenburg">House of Mecklenburg</a> was settled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hamburg-1701">Treaty of Hamburg</a> in 1701. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-duke-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">Frederick William</a> received the larger western share as the Duchy of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg-Schwerin</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwerin">Schwerin</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-rostock">Rostock</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wismar">Wismar's</a> hinterland, while a smaller share became Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty descended from the Obotrite prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niklot">Niklot</a> of the 12th century. Under the 1755 settlement with the estates, power was shared with the knighthood, preserving large noble estates and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> until 1820. The economy rested on grain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>. Frederick Francis I joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> and became grand duke in 1815. A liberal constitution of 1849 was annulled in 1850, and the old estates constitution remained in force until 1918.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg-Schwerin</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-german-confederation">North German Confederation</a> and in 1871 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-francis-iv-grand-duke-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">Grand Duke Frederick Francis IV</a> abdicated in November 1918, and the state continued as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">Free State of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-mecklenburg-schwerin.jpg" alt="Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Gro%C3%9Fherzogt%C3%BCmer_Mecklenburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1701 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Schwerin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick William, Frederick Francis I, Frederick Francis IV</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=duchy-of-mecklenburg-schwerin" aria-label="Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4934 335 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5254 591L5254 591M5254 591L5229 694M5254 591L5199 691M5254 591L5300 622M5254 591L5254 591"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5254 591h0M5229 694h0M5199 691h0M5300 622h0M5254 591h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5254 591h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5254 591h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Schwerin. <a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=duchy-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
